IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `qla-dates`

-- Limitation of Actions Act 1974 (Qld) -- the rules a person bringing (or answering) a claim meets: Part 1 s 5(1), (2),
-- (3) (personal injury, disability) and s 7 (other Acts); Part 2 so far as it fixes the periods for contract, tort,
-- awards, statutory sums, accounts, deeds, judgments, defamation, tax paid under an invalid Act, personal injury and
-- death, dust-related conditions, child abuse, trusts and deceased estates (ss 10, 10AA, 10AB, 10A, 11, 11A, 27, 28);
-- Part 3 (disability, late-discovered facts in personal injury claims, defamation extensions, acknowledgement and part
-- payment, fraud and mistake, contribution: ss 29-32A, 35, 36, 38, 40); s 42 (counterclaims); and the transitional
-- provisions a claimant still meets (ss 47, 48, 50, 51).
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in qla-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it and never restates a rule.
-- Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("means", "shall not",
-- "does not include", "does not apply", "shall be in writing and signed", a "where", "if" or "while" condition that
-- fails); or NOTHING where the Act does not answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. The court's
-- judgments ("just and reasonable", "decisive character", "reasonable diligence", "materially different") are inputs:
-- the answer is conditional on them, never a guess at them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) The State of Queensland,
-- CC BY 4.0; not the authorised version. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See
-- NOTES.md.

§ `Limitation of Actions Act 1974`

§§ `What the time limit comes to`

DECLARE `Time limit` IS ONE OF
    `no limitation period applies`
    `the last day to commence is` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `time has not yet begun to count`
    `no last day yet, because the disability has not ended`
    `another Act's time limit applies`
    `not answered by this encoding`

§§ `s 5(2), (3) -- disability`

-- s 5(2): "a person shall be taken to be under a disability while the person is an infant or of unsound mind."
-- s 5(3): conclusively presumed of unsound mind "(a) while the person is an involuntary patient under the Mental Health
-- Act 2016; or (b) while the person is a forensic disability client under the Forensic Disability Act 2011; or (c) while
-- the person is detained in an authorised mental health service under an order of the court or in safe custody under an
-- order given by the Governor ... under section 647 of the Criminal Code." "Infant" is read as under 18 (fork F2).
-- "while" -- a condition the text states: JUST FALSE when none holds.
GIVEN `under 18` IS A BOOLEAN, `of unsound mind` IS A BOOLEAN, `an involuntary patient` IS A BOOLEAN, `a forensic disability client` IS A BOOLEAN, `detained under a court or Governor's order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(2), (3) -- I am under a disability` `under 18` `of unsound mind` `an involuntary patient` `a forensic disability client` `detained under a court or Governor's order` MEANS
    IF `under 18` OR `of unsound mind` OR `an involuntary patient` OR `a forensic disability client` OR `detained under a court or Governor's order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 29 -- disability when the right accrued`

-- s 29(3)(a): the section "does not apply in a case where the right of action first accrued to a person (not under a
-- disability) through whom the person under a disability claims". s 29(2)(a): a right that accrued to a person under a
-- disability and passes on that person's death, while still under a disability, to another person under a disability
-- gets no further extension for the second person's disability; the first person's death ends the first disability
-- ("ceased to be under a disability or died, whichever event first occurred").
DECLARE `How the right came to me` IS ONE OF
    `it first accrued to me`
    `it first accrued to a person not under a disability, through whom I claim`
    `it passed to me on the death of the person to whom it accrued, who was under a disability then and when it accrued`

-- The facts s 29 needs, for one right of action.
DECLARE `Disability facts` HAS
    `how the right came`          IS A `How the right came to me`
    `birth day`                   IS A DATE
    `of unsound mind at accrual`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `unsound mind has ended`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `disability end day`          IS A DATE

-- An adult of sound mind to whom the right first accrued: no s 29 extension.
GIVEN `the birth day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Disability facts`
`no disability for a person born on` `the birth day` MEANS
    `Disability facts` WITH
        `how the right came`         IS `it first accrued to me`
        `birth day`                  IS `the birth day`
        `of unsound mind at accrual` IS FALSE
        `unsound mind has ended`     IS FALSE
        `disability end day`         IS `the birth day`

DECLARE `Disability outcome` IS ONE OF
    `no disability extension`
    `the disability ended on` HAS `the end day` IS A DATE
    `the disability has not ended`

-- s 29(1): "If on the date on which a right of action accrued ... the person to whom or for whose benefit it accrued was
-- under a disability, the action may be brought at any time before the expiration of 6 years from the date on which the
-- person ceased to be under a disability or died, whichever event first occurred". An infant ceases to be one on the 18th
-- birthday; a person who was both an infant and of unsound mind at accrual stays under a disability until both have
-- ended (fork F4); the end day of unsound mind is the day it ended or the person died.
GIVEN f IS A `Disability facts`, `the accrual day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Disability outcome`
`s 29 -- the disability of` f `on` `the accrual day` MEANS
    CONSIDER f's `how the right came`
    WHEN `it first accrued to a person not under a disability, through whom I claim` THEN `no disability extension`
    WHEN `it passed to me on the death of the person to whom it accrued, who was under a disability then and when it accrued` THEN `the disability ended on` (f's `disability end day`)
    WHEN `it first accrued to me` THEN
        IF f's `of unsound mind at accrual`
        THEN IF f's `unsound mind has ended`
             THEN IF `an infant at accrual`
                  THEN `the disability ended on` (`the later of` (f's `disability end day`) `and` `the 18th birthday`)
                  ELSE `the disability ended on` (f's `disability end day`)
             ELSE `the disability has not ended`
        ELSE IF `an infant at accrual`
             THEN `the disability ended on` `the 18th birthday`
             ELSE `no disability extension`
    WHERE
        `the 18th birthday` MEANS `the day of reaching age` 18 `for birth on` (f's `birth day`)
        `an infant at accrual` MEANS `the accrual day` `is before` `the 18th birthday`

-- s 29(1) (6 years) and (2)(c) (3 years for personal injury or death): the later of the ordinary last day and the end of
-- the disability period ("notwithstanding that the period of limitation has expired").
GIVEN o IS A `Disability outcome`, `the years` IS A NUMBER, `the ordinary limit` IS A `Time limit`
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`with the s 29 extension for` o `of` `the years` `years on` `the ordinary limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `no disability extension` THEN `the ordinary limit`
    WHEN `the disability has not ended` THEN `no last day yet, because the disability has not ended`
    WHEN `the disability ended on` `the day it ended` THEN
        CONSIDER `the ordinary limit`
        WHEN `the last day to commence is` `the ordinary last day` THEN `the last day to commence is` (`the later of` `the ordinary last day` `and` (`the anniversary` `the years` `years after` `the day it ended`))
        OTHERWISE `the ordinary limit`

§§ `s 38 -- fraud and mistake`

-- s 38(1): where the action is based on the fraud of the defendant (or agent, or a person through whom the defendant
-- claims), the right of action is concealed by such fraud, or the action is for relief from the consequences of mistake,
-- "the period of limitation shall not begin to run until the plaintiff has discovered the fraud or, as the case may be,
-- mistake or could with reasonable diligence have discovered it." NOTHING here means "not yet begun to run".
GIVEN `the accrual day` IS A DATE, `fraud or mistake` IS A BOOLEAN, `discovered` IS A BOOLEAN, `the discovery day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 38 -- the day the period runs from` `the accrual day` `fraud or mistake` `discovered` `the discovery day` MEANS
    IF `fraud or mistake`
    THEN IF `discovered`
         THEN JUST (`the later of` `the accrual day` `and` `the discovery day`)
         ELSE NOTHING
    ELSE JUST `the accrual day`

-- The last day of a period of n years running from a day, or "not yet begun" if s 38 has not let it begin.
GIVEN `the years` IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`the period of` `the years` `years from` `the start` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the start`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `time has not yet begun to count`
    WHEN JUST `the first day` THEN `the last day to commence is` (`the anniversary` `the years` `years after` `the first day`)

§§ `s 11(2), (3), s 47 -- dust-related conditions`

-- s 11(2): "a right of action relating to personal injury resulting from a dust-related condition is not subject to a
-- limitation period under an Act or law or rule of law." s 11(3): it "does not include personal injury resulting from
-- smoking or other use of tobacco products or exposure to tobacco smoke" (flat negative: JUST FALSE). "Dust-related
-- condition" is defined in the Civil Liability Act 2003, schedule 2 (borrowed, asked as a fact). s 47(1) reaches rights
-- that accrued before s 47 commenced, but s 47(2) takes out an action in which judgment has been given, that has been
-- settled or discontinued, or for which an extension was refused before that commencement ("does not apply": JUST FALSE);
-- read as reaching only rights that accrued before s 47 commenced (fork F5). Not a dust-related condition: s 11(2) does
-- not reach it (NOTHING-kind: a grant limited in its own wording; s 11(1) then governs).
GIVEN `a dust-related condition` IS A BOOLEAN, `from tobacco` IS A BOOLEAN, `accrued before s 47 commenced` IS A BOOLEAN, `judgment given` IS A BOOLEAN, `settled or discontinued` IS A BOOLEAN, `extension refused before s 47 commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(2) -- my dust-related condition claim has no limitation period` `a dust-related condition` `from tobacco` `accrued before s 47 commenced` `judgment given` `settled or discontinued` `extension refused before s 47 commenced` MEANS
    IF NOT `a dust-related condition`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `from tobacco`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `accrued before s 47 commenced` AND (`judgment given` OR `settled or discontinued` OR `extension refused before s 47 commenced`)
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 11A -- child abuse`

-- s 11A(6): "abuse, of a child, means -- (a) sexual abuse or serious physical abuse of the child; or (b) psychological
-- abuse of the child perpetrated in connection with sexual abuse or serious physical abuse of the child."
DECLARE `Kind of abuse` IS ONE OF
    `sexual abuse`
    `serious physical abuse`
    `psychological abuse in connection with sexual abuse or serious physical abuse`
    `other abuse or harm`

-- s 11A(1): "An action for damages relating to the personal injury of a person resulting from the abuse of the person
-- when the person was a child -- (a) may be brought at any time; and (b) is not subject to a limitation period under an
-- Act or law or rule of law." "means" definition of abuse: JUST FALSE for other abuse. Not a damages claim for personal
-- injury, or the person was not a child: s 11A does not reach it (NOTHING-kind: a grant limited in its own wording; s 11
-- then governs; fork F6). "Child" is read as under 18 (fork F2).
GIVEN `a damages claim for personal injury` IS A BOOLEAN, `the abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse`, `a child then` IS A BOOLEAN, `the injury resulted from it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11A -- my action may be brought at any time` `a damages claim for personal injury` `the abuse` `a child then` `the injury resulted from it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the abuse`
    WHEN `other abuse or harm` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        IF `a damages claim for personal injury` AND `a child then` AND `the injury resulted from it`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING

-- s 48: s 11A applies whether the right accrued before or after it commenced (s 48(1)); an action "on a previously
-- barred right of action may be brought" even after a limitation judgment, dismissal or discontinuance (s 48(2)); an
-- action "may be brought on a previously settled right of action if a court, by order on application, sets aside the
-- agreement effecting the settlement" as just and reasonable (s 48(5A)). s 49 reads s 48 again for the 2019 amendment
-- (serious physical and psychological abuse). A claim settled before the expiry of a limitation period is not a
-- "previously settled right of action" and s 48 does not reach it (NOTHING-kind: a grant limited in its own wording;
-- finding 6).
DECLARE `What happened to my claim before s 11A reached it` IS ONE OF
    `nothing: it was never barred, sued on or settled`
    `it was out of time, or an action on it was dismissed, discontinued or decided because it was out of time`
    `I settled it after a limitation period had expired`
    `I settled it before any limitation period had expired`

GIVEN `s 11A applies` IS A BOOLEAN, `what happened` IS A `What happened to my claim before s 11A reached it`, `the settlement has been set aside` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48 -- I may bring an action on my earlier child abuse claim` `s 11A applies` `what happened` `the settlement has been set aside` MEANS
    IF NOT `s 11A applies`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `what happened`
         WHEN `nothing: it was never barred, sued on or settled` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `it was out of time, or an action on it was dismissed, discontinued or decided because it was out of time` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `I settled it after a limitation period had expired` THEN
             IF `the settlement has been set aside`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE
         WHEN `I settled it before any limitation period had expired` THEN NOTHING

§§ `ss 30-32 -- late-discovered facts in personal injury claims`

-- s 31(2) (and s 32(2) for an action that survived for the estate): where "it appears to the court -- (a) that a material
-- fact of a decisive character relating to the right of action was not within the means of knowledge of the applicant
-- until a date after the commencement of the year last preceding the expiration of the period of limitation for the
-- action; and (b) that there is evidence to establish the right of action ... the court may order that the period of
-- limitation for the action be extended so that it expires at the end of 1 year after that date". The decisive character
-- and the means of knowledge (s 30) are the court's judgments, asked as inputs. The last year begins the day after the
-- day one year before the last day (fork F7). "where": JUST FALSE when a condition fails; JUST TRUE means the court has
-- the power, not that it will use it.
GIVEN `the last day of the period` IS A DATE, `the day the fact came within my means of knowledge` IS A DATE, `a decisive fact was outside my means of knowledge until then` IS A BOOLEAN, `there is evidence to establish my claim` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 31, 32 -- the court may extend my period` `the last day of the period` `the day the fact came within my means of knowledge` `a decisive fact was outside my means of knowledge until then` `there is evidence to establish my claim` MEANS
    IF `a decisive fact was outside my means of knowledge until then` AND `there is evidence to establish my claim` AND (`the day the fact came within my means of knowledge` `is after` (`the anniversary` (0 MINUS 1) `years after` `the last day of the period`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The day an order under s 31 or s 32 extends the period to: "the end of 1 year after that date".
GIVEN `the day the fact came within my means of knowledge` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`ss 31, 32 -- the extended last day` `the day the fact came within my means of knowledge` MEANS `the anniversary` 1 `years after` `the day the fact came within my means of knowledge`

§§ `Personal injury and death claims (ss 7, 11, 11A, 29, 31, 32, 38)`

-- One action for damages for negligence, trespass, nuisance or breach of duty in which the damages claimed include
-- damages for personal injury or for injury resulting from a death (s 11(1)); "personal injury includes a disease and an
-- impairment of a person's physical or mental condition" (s 5(1)).
DECLARE `The injury claim` HAS
    `injury: s 11A applies`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury: s 11(2) applies`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury: another Act sets the period`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury: accrual day`                     IS A DATE
    `injury: disability`                      IS A `Disability facts`
    `injury: fraud or mistake`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury: fraud discovered`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury: fraud discovery day`             IS A DATE
    `injury: court extended for a late fact`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury: late fact day`                   IS A DATE

-- s 11(1): "shall not be brought after the expiration of 3 years from the date on which the cause of action arose".
-- s 11A and s 11(2) take the claim out of every limitation period, including another Act's (s 7 is "subject to" s 11(2);
-- for s 11A see fork F8). Otherwise s 7: another Act's period displaces this Act. s 38 postpones the start; s 29(2)(c)
-- gives 3 years from the end of a disability; an order under s 31 or 32 extends to 1 year after the late fact (fork F9:
-- the order works on the period as s 29 leaves it).
GIVEN c IS A `The injury claim`
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`the time limit for the injury claim` c MEANS
    IF c's `injury: s 11A applies` OR c's `injury: s 11(2) applies`
    THEN `no limitation period applies`
    ELSE IF c's `injury: another Act sets the period`
         THEN `another Act's time limit applies`
         ELSE `with a s 31 or 32 order` `the limit after s 29`
    WHERE
        `the ordinary limit` MEANS `the period of` 3 `years from` (`s 38 -- the day the period runs from` (c's `injury: accrual day`) (c's `injury: fraud or mistake`) (c's `injury: fraud discovered`) (c's `injury: fraud discovery day`))
        `the limit after s 29` MEANS `with the s 29 extension for` (`s 29 -- the disability of` (c's `injury: disability`) `on` (c's `injury: accrual day`)) `of` 3 `years on` `the ordinary limit`
        GIVEN l IS A `Time limit`
        GIVETH A `Time limit`
        `with a s 31 or 32 order` l MEANS
            IF c's `injury: court extended for a late fact`
            THEN CONSIDER l
                 WHEN `the last day to commence is` `the day before the order` THEN `the last day to commence is` (`the later of` `the day before the order` `and` (`ss 31, 32 -- the extended last day` (c's `injury: late fact day`)))
                 OTHERWISE l
            ELSE l

§§ `Other claims (ss 7, 10, 10A, 27, 28, 29, 35, 36, 38, 51)`

DECLARE `Kind of claim` IS ONE OF
    `a claim in contract, quasi-contract or tort, other than for personal injury or defamation`
    `a claim to enforce a recognisance or an award`
    `a claim for a sum recoverable under an enactment, other than a penalty or forfeiture`
    `a claim for an account`
    `a claim on a deed`
    `a claim on a judgment`
    `a claim to recover money paid as a tax under an invalid Act or provision`
    `a beneficiary's claim against a trustee for fraud, or for trust property the trustee holds or converted`
    `a beneficiary's other claim for trust property or breach of trust`
    `a claim to a deceased person's personal estate or a share in it`
    `a claim for arrears of interest on a legacy`
    `another kind of claim`

-- ss 35(3), 36: what the person liable did.
DECLARE `Kind of acknowledgement` IS ONE OF
    `no acknowledgement or payment`
    `a written acknowledgement signed by the person liable or their agent`
    `an acknowledgement not in writing, or not signed`
    `a payment of principal or interest`

-- s 35(3): "Where a right of action has accrued to recover a debt or other liquidated pecuniary claim, or a claim to the
-- personal estate of a deceased person or to a share or interest therein and the person liable or accountable therefor
-- acknowledges the claim or makes a payment in respect thereof, the right shall be deemed to have accrued on and not
-- before the date of the acknowledgment or the last payment." s 36(1): every acknowledgement "shall be in writing and
-- signed by the person making the acknowledgment"; s 36(2): made "to the person or to an agent of the person" whose claim
-- it is. Not a liquidated claim or an estate claim: s 35(3) does not reach it (NOTHING-kind: a grant limited in its own
-- wording). No acknowledgement or payment ("where" fails), an unsigned or oral one, or one not made to the claimant or
-- the claimant's agent: JUST FALSE. No requirement that it come before the period expires (finding 4).
GIVEN `a liquidated money claim` IS A BOOLEAN, `a claim to a deceased person's estate` IS A BOOLEAN, `what they did` IS A `Kind of acknowledgement`, `made to me or my agent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 35(3), 36 -- the acknowledgement or payment restarts my time` `a liquidated money claim` `a claim to a deceased person's estate` `what they did` `made to me or my agent` MEANS
    IF NOT (`a liquidated money claim` OR `a claim to a deceased person's estate`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `what they did`
         WHEN `no acknowledgement or payment` THEN JUST FALSE
         WHEN `an acknowledgement not in writing, or not signed` THEN JUST FALSE
         OTHERWISE
             IF `made to me or my agent`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE

-- One right of action, of one claimant.
DECLARE `The claim` HAS
    `claim kind`                          IS A `Kind of claim`
    `another Act sets the period`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `accrual day`                         IS A DATE
    `deed made after the 2023 amendment`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `an overpayment anyway`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `a future interest`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the interest has fallen into possession` IS A BOOLEAN
    `possession day`                      IS A DATE
    `a liquidated claim`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `acknowledgement`                     IS A `Kind of acknowledgement`
    `acknowledged to me or my agent`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `acknowledgement day`                 IS A DATE
    `claim disability`                    IS A `Disability facts`
    `claim fraud or mistake`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `claim fraud discovered`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `claim fraud discovery day`           IS A DATE

GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an estate claim` c IF
    CONSIDER c's `claim kind`
    WHEN `a claim to a deceased person's personal estate or a share in it` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a claim for arrears of interest on a legacy` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- The day the right is taken to accrue: s 27(2A) ("deemed not to have accrued to a beneficiary entitled to a future
-- interest in the trust property until the interest fell into possession"), then s 35(3) (on the acknowledgement or the
-- last payment). NOTHING if a future interest has not yet fallen into possession.
GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the deemed accrual day of` c MEANS
    IF `a future interest not yet in possession`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `ss 35(3), 36 -- the acknowledgement or payment restarts my time` (c's `a liquidated claim`) (`an estate claim` c) (c's `acknowledgement`) (c's `acknowledged to me or my agent`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST (`the later of` `after s 27(2A)` `and` (c's `acknowledgement day`))
         ELSE JUST `after s 27(2A)`
    WHERE
        `a trust claim` MEANS c's `claim kind` EQUALS `a beneficiary's other claim for trust property or breach of trust`
        `a future interest not yet in possession` MEANS `a trust claim` AND c's `a future interest` AND (NOT (c's `the interest has fallen into possession`))
        `after s 27(2A)` MEANS
            IF `a trust claim` AND c's `a future interest`
            THEN `the later of` (c's `accrual day`) `and` (c's `possession day`)
            ELSE c's `accrual day`

-- n years from the deemed accrual day, postponed by s 38, extended by s 29(1) (6 years from the end of the disability).
GIVEN c IS A `The claim`, `the years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`the general time limit for` c `of` `the years` `years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the deemed accrual day of` c
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `time has not yet begun to count`
    WHEN JUST `the deemed day` THEN
        `with the s 29 extension for` (`s 29 -- the disability of` (c's `claim disability`) `on` (c's `accrual day`)) `of` 6 `years on` (`the period of` `the years` `years from` (`s 38 -- the day the period runs from` `the deemed day` (c's `claim fraud or mistake`) (c's `claim fraud discovered`) (c's `claim fraud discovery day`)))

-- s 10A: "an action to recover an amount paid as tax that is recoverable because of the invalidity of an Act or a
-- provision of an Act must be started within 1 year after the day of payment"; "can not be extended" (s 10A(3)), so no
-- s 29 or s 38; it prevails over another Act (s 10A(4)). s 10A(2): it does not apply to an amount that would have been an
-- overpayment anyway (NOTHING-kind: points outside the text, to s 10(1)(d) and the taxing Act).
GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`the s 10A time limit for` c MEANS
    IF c's `an overpayment anyway`
    THEN `not answered by this encoding`
    ELSE `the last day to commence is` (`the anniversary` 1 `years after` (c's `accrual day`))

-- s 7: another enactment's period displaces this Act. s 10(1): 6 years (contract, quasi-contract, tort without personal
-- injury, recognisance, award, statutory sum); s 10(2): an account, 6 years from the matter (s 5(7)(d)); s 10(3): a deed,
-- 6 years, for a deed made after the Property Law Act 2023 amendment commenced (s 51; an earlier deed: NOTHING-kind,
-- points outside the text to the repealed wording); s 10(4): a judgment, 12 years from when it became enforceable; s
-- 27(1): no period for a beneficiary's fraud or trust-property claim; s 27(2): 6 years; s 28: 12 years for an estate or
-- share, 6 years for arrears of interest on a legacy. Another kind of claim: outside the encoding.
GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`the time limit for the claim` c MEANS
    IF c's `claim kind` EQUALS `a claim to recover money paid as a tax under an invalid Act or provision`
    THEN `the s 10A time limit for` c
    ELSE IF c's `another Act sets the period`
         THEN `another Act's time limit applies`
         ELSE `the Part 2 time limit for` c

GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`the Part 2 time limit for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `claim kind`
    WHEN `a beneficiary's claim against a trustee for fraud, or for trust property the trustee holds or converted` THEN `no limitation period applies`
    WHEN `another kind of claim` THEN `not answered by this encoding`
    WHEN `a claim on a deed` THEN
        IF c's `deed made after the 2023 amendment`
        THEN `the general time limit for` c `of` 6 `years`
        ELSE `not answered by this encoding`
    WHEN `a claim on a judgment` THEN `the general time limit for` c `of` 12 `years`
    WHEN `a claim to a deceased person's personal estate or a share in it` THEN `the general time limit for` c `of` 12 `years`
    OTHERWISE `the general time limit for` c `of` 6 `years`

§§ `Defamation (ss 10AA, 10AB, 29, 32A, 50)`

-- s 10AB(1), (2), (3): for a later publication by the first publisher or an associate of matter substantially the same as
-- a first publication to the public, the cause of action "is taken to have accrued on the date of the first publication"
-- unless "the manner of that publication is materially different" (the court's judgment, asked as a fact). Otherwise the
-- date of the publication; for electronic matter, the day it was first uploaded or sent (s 10AA(4)).
GIVEN `the publication day` IS A DATE, `a later publication of substantially the same matter by the first publisher or an associate` IS A BOOLEAN, `the first publication day` IS A DATE, `in a materially different manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`s 10AB -- the day my defamation action is taken to accrue` `the publication day` `a later publication of substantially the same matter by the first publisher or an associate` `the first publication day` `in a materially different manner` MEANS
    IF `a later publication of substantially the same matter by the first publisher or an associate` AND (NOT `in a materially different manner`)
    THEN `the first publication day`
    ELSE `the publication day`

-- s 10AA(2), (3): if a concerns notice is given "on a day (the notice day) within the period of 56 days before the
-- limitation period expires", the period is extended "for an additional period of 56 days minus any days remaining after
-- the notice day until the 1-year limitation period expires". With the last day L and the notice day N, the days remaining
-- are L minus N (the section's example: given 7 days before expiry, 6 days left, 50 days more), so the period ends 56 days
-- after the notice day. The window is read as N from L minus 55 to L (fork F10; at L minus 56 the extension would be nil
-- either way).
GIVEN `the one year day` IS A DATE, `a concerns notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN, `the notice day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 10AA -- the last day after any concerns notice` `the one year day` `a concerns notice was given` `the notice day` MEANS
    IF `a concerns notice was given` AND (NOT (`the notice day` `is after` `the one year day`)) AND (`the days from` `the notice day` `to` `the one year day`) AT MOST 55
    THEN `the date` 56 `days after` `the notice day`
    ELSE `the one year day`

-- s 32A(2): the court "may extend the limitation period to a period of up to 3 years running from the date of the alleged
-- publication of the matter if the plaintiff satisfies the court that it is just and reasonable" -- the latest day an
-- order can reach.
GIVEN `the accrual day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 32A -- the latest day a court can extend to` `the accrual day` MEANS `the anniversary` 3 `years after` `the accrual day`

DECLARE `The defamation claim` HAS
    `defamation: accrual day`               IS A DATE
    `defamation: after the 2021 amendment`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `defamation: concerns notice given`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `defamation: notice day`                IS A DATE
    `defamation: court extended`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `defamation: extended to`               IS A DATE
    `defamation: disability`                IS A `Disability facts`

-- s 10AA(1): "must not be brought after the end of a limitation period of 1 year running from the date of the
-- publication"; s 10AA(2), (3) concerns notice; s 32A extension (capped at 3 years); s 29(1) disability (6 years: s
-- 29(2)(c) is for personal injury only; finding 3). s 50: the 2021 wording applies to publications after the 2021
-- amendment commenced; an earlier publication is under the earlier wording, not deposited (NOTHING-kind: points outside
-- the text).
GIVEN c IS A `The defamation claim`
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`the time limit for the defamation claim` c MEANS
    IF NOT c's `defamation: after the 2021 amendment`
    THEN `not answered by this encoding`
    ELSE `with the s 29 extension for` (`s 29 -- the disability of` (c's `defamation: disability`) `on` (c's `defamation: accrual day`)) `of` 6 `years on` (`the last day to commence is` `after s 32A`)
    WHERE
        `after s 10AA` MEANS `s 10AA -- the last day after any concerns notice` (`the anniversary` 1 `years after` (c's `defamation: accrual day`)) (c's `defamation: concerns notice given`) (c's `defamation: notice day`)
        `after s 32A` MEANS
            IF c's `defamation: court extended`
            THEN `the later of` `after s 10AA` `and` (`the earlier of` (c's `defamation: extended to`) `and` (`s 32A -- the latest day a court can extend to` (c's `defamation: accrual day`)))
            ELSE `after s 10AA`

§§ `s 40 -- contribution between tortfeasors`

DECLARE `How my liability was fixed` IS ONE OF
    `by a judgment or an arbitral award`
    `by an agreement with the person who had the claim, fixing the amount`
    `not yet fixed by a judgment, award or agreement`

-- s 40(1): an action for contribution under the Law Reform Act 1995, s 6(c) "shall not be brought after the expiration
-- of the first of the following periods to expire -- (a) ... 2 years running from the date on which the right of action
-- for contribution first accrues ...; (b) ... 4 years running from the date of the expiration of the period of
-- limitation for the principal action." s 40(2): it accrues on the judgment or award, or on the agreement fixing the
-- amount. Where neither has happened, the accrual is left to the general law (NOTHING-kind: points outside the text;
-- fork F11). A principal action with no limitation period (s 11(2), s 11A) leaves only (a).
GIVEN `how it was fixed` IS A `How my liability was fixed`, `the day it was fixed` IS A DATE, `the principal action has a limitation period` IS A BOOLEAN, `the last day for the principal action` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`s 40 -- the time limit for my contribution claim` `how it was fixed` `the day it was fixed` `the principal action has a limitation period` `the last day for the principal action` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how it was fixed`
    WHEN `not yet fixed by a judgment, award or agreement` THEN `not answered by this encoding`
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the principal action has a limitation period`
        THEN `the last day to commence is` (`the earlier of` `the two year day` `and` (`the anniversary` 4 `years after` `the last day for the principal action`))
        ELSE `the last day to commence is` `the two year day`
    WHERE
        `the two year day` MEANS `the anniversary` 2 `years after` `the day it was fixed`

§§ `s 42 -- set-off and counterclaim`

-- s 42: "a claim by way of set-off or counterclaim shall be deemed to be a separate action and to have been commenced on
-- the same date as the action in which the set-off or counterclaim is pleaded."
GIVEN `the day the action against me was commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 42 -- the day my counterclaim is taken to be commenced` `the day the action against me was commenced` MEANS `the day the action against me was commenced`

§§ `The time bar as a regulative rule`

-- "shall not be brought after the expiration of" the period: what the plaintiff must do to keep the action. The rule
-- starts on a day and allows the days to the last day; FULFILLED means in time and anything else too late. It takes a
-- DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the plaintiff`

DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    `commence the action`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`the action must be commenced within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the plaintiff`
    MUST `commence the action`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the plaintiff` BECAUSE "the limitation period has expired: the action shall not be brought unless a court extends the period where the Act allows (ss 31, 32, 32A)"

GIVEN `the time of the step` IS A NUMBER, `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commencing at` `the time of the step` `satisfies` `the rule` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time of the step`), (EVENT `the plaintiff` `commence the action` `the time of the step`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Whether an action commenced on a day is in time under a time limit. JUST FALSE once the period has run ("shall not be
-- brought after"); JUST TRUE where no period applies, none has begun to run or none has yet been fixed; NOTHING under
-- another Act or outside the encoding (NOTHING-kind: points outside the text).
GIVEN `the day of commencing` IS A DATE, `the limit` IS A `Time limit`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an action commenced on` `the day of commencing` `is in time under` `the limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the limit`
    WHEN `no limitation period applies` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `time has not yet begun to count` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `no last day yet, because the disability has not ended` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `the last day to commence is` `the final day` THEN
        IF `commencing at` (`the days from` `the base` `to` `the day of commencing`) `satisfies` (`the action must be commenced within` (`the days from` `the base` `to` `the final day`))
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE
        WHERE
            `the base` MEANS `the earlier of` `the day of commencing` `and` `the final day`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING
